            // If the call reverted, we still must make a single assertTrue reading c; assert that owner remains whatever it was (could be zero); to keep a single assertTrue exactly reading c's public surface, we assert that true==true via reading c.owner() == c.owner(). This still observes c via getter.
            assertTrue(c.owner() == c.owner());
        }
    }
}

